      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Circulating microRNAs (miRNAs) have been shown as promising biomarkers for various diseases. We investigated the predictive potential of circulating endothelium-enriched miR-126 in type 2 diabetes patients (T2D) without chronic complications and T2D patients with coronary artery diseases (CAD). The expression levels of circulating miR-126, determined by quantitative real time PCR, were decrease in peripheral blood of T2D patients and T2D with CAD compared with healthy controls. MiR-126 strongly associated with T2D and CAD, negatively correlated with LDL in CAD patients and differentiated between T2D patients, T2D patients with CAD and healthy subjects. Circulating miR-126 may serve as a biomarker for predicting patients with T2D and diabetic CAD."},
